WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.000
- The Facebook Oversight
Board has reaffirmed

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.440
its decision to ban former
president Trump from Facebook

00:00:05.440 --> 00:00:06.330
causing lots of people

00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.350
to have really, really
terrible legal takes

00:00:08.350 --> 00:00:10.240
including some saying
that the Supreme Court

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:12.110
should overrule Facebook's decision.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:13.470
Now a couple of things.

00:00:13.470 --> 00:00:15.650
Number one, that's not a thing.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.300
You can't appeal a decision
of a non-governmental body

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.300
that's not a court to the Supreme Court,

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:23.060
that's just not a thing.

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.380
And then number two,

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.390
a lot of people talk about Section 230

00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.790
saying this is big tech

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.490
and Section 230 allows them
to do that, that's not true.

00:00:30.490 --> 00:00:32.400
The thing that allows
Facebook to discriminate

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.430
who is on its platform and
what speeches on that platform

00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.330
is the first amendment.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:39.520
You can control who talks in your house

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:42.020
and what speech you wanna
hear in your own house.

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.170
It's not Section 230,
it's the first amendment.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.353
So we won't be seeing these guys in court.

